+# P0–P6 implementation and acceptance matrix
+
+This is a concrete engineering plan, **not** a statement that the work is already merged.
+
+| Phase | Engineering deliverable | Mandatory executable or independent evidence | Default state |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| P0 | Frozen main SHA + PR/branch candidate matrix, live-authority directed graph | HEAD, base, blob hashes; every authority write traced back to its signer/role; proof of inactive path where claimed | NOT VERIFIED |
+| P1 | Typed authorization envelope + one verified policy engine for account/task/Hepta/provider/upgrade/recovery | Domain separation, PQ ownership anchored, explicit `pq-only` or `hybrid-and`; adversarial negative tests at each ingress and final state mutation | NOT VERIFIED |
+| P2 | Rotation/epoch/cutover and anti-downgrade | Classic-only rejected post-cutover; unknown algorithm rejected; hybrid signature stripping and key misbinding tests; inactive legacy format no authority | NOT VERIFIED |
+| P3 | Live proof system PQ-128 review and W1 candidate qualification | Guest/program digest, recursion/transcript/FRI/FS model, independently validated quantum soundness >= 128, real invalid proof rejection, Groth16 route closed | NOT VERIFIED |
+| P4 | Complete PoN cheapest-legal-solver security | Optimized classical and quantum search on the *valid* relation; low-rank/matrix/batch/precompute; worst-case invalid proof; difficulty/fork-choice attack replay | NOT VERIFIED |
+| P5 | Snapshot, reorg, rollback and revocation resilience | External monotonic anchor or explicitly accepted external trust model; multi-crash tests; restart/reorg/deep fork; key revocation cannot be rolled back | NOT VERIFIED |
+| P6 | Network capacity / DoS + independent replay/sign-off | Real node network and malformed input budgets; peak RSS, verification p99, propagation, block sizes, WAL/restore; third-party review tied to exact SHA | NOT VERIFIED |
+
+## Suggested source-specific code tasks after the actual repo becomes readable
+
+**P0: enumerate actual authority writes.** Search node ingress, task V5, Hepta admission/handoff, Cell provider discovery, model publishing, validator/finality, governance and recovery. Record whether each Ed25519 usage is test-only, historical read-only or active authority. Do not do broad blind `ed25519 -> ml_dsa` replacements: wire format and key lifecycle change.
+
+**P1/P2: implement versioned canonical authorization.** New domain-separated signed envelope should carry chain ID, subject ID, role, keyset digest, policy version, epoch, nonce, event digest, expiry and explicit mode. Centralize verify-to-authorize to remove duplicate legacy fallback. Tests must call real ingress or authorization APIs, not only policy helper functions. A valid ML-DSA signature is insufficient if it has the wrong role, chain, epoch or key registration.
+
+**P3: freeze exactly what W1 proves.** Lock guest image/verifier binary, transcript and recursive composition. A W1 manifest's `production_consensus_activation=false` should remain fail-closed until cryptographic and operational qualification. The code must distinguish research/test receipts from consensus finality receipts, with no Groth16, Fake or untrusted remote receipt accepted as substitutes.
+
+**P4: adversarial solver baseline.** Generate families of legal/invalid witnesses and include preprocessing costs amortized across multiple challenges. Profile real optimized solutions under identical hardware/energy/latency budgets. For quantum analysis, count reversible oracle synthesis, error correction overhead, memory access, uncomputation and end-to-end block creation. Test timestamp manipulation, difficulty transition boundaries and cumulative-work fork choice. Treat any unbounded upper estimate as **not** proof of a lower bound.
+
+**P5: externally anchored restoration.** Persist key rotation and cutover state in a replayable, signed journal but do not trust an entirely self-contained old snapshot as proof of current epoch. Include a separately protected monotonic anchor/certified checkpoint and reject backwards moves unless an explicit disaster-recovery protocol authorizes them.
+
+**P6: capacity limits.** Verify maximum accepted sizes *before* heavy cryptographic work when safe, use bounded allocations, peer abuse controls, peer reputation not as sole security, and measured rejection CPU. Record p95/p99 and worst invalid input, not just happy-path throughput.
+
+## Required negative test checklist
+
+- Classic valid / PQ missing; classic valid / PQ malformed; PQ valid / classic missing in a hybrid epoch.
+- Disagreeing signer keysets; signature stripped/downgraded; unknown algorithm tag; legacy version reinterpreted.
+- Replay in same chain, different chain ID, old epoch, future version, changed role and key rotation.
+- Candidate verifier bound to wrong guest image, wrong public journal, wrong transcript/config, wrong recursion code, Groth16 compression substituted.
+- Malformed/oversize ML-DSA signature, public key, proof and witness; exhaustion across 10k repeated invalid requests.
+- Timestamp and difficulty adversarial forks, private branch withheld, deep reorg, cheapest structured matrices and multi-challenge preprocessing.
+- DB restored to old valid snapshot, rollback to revoked key, power loss before/after anchor persistence, chain state ahead of external anchor.
+
+## Explicit unverified blockers to report on every release review
+
+1. Current HEAD and deployment configuration unknown? **No release qualification.**
+2. Any active authority signable with classic-only? **No whole-chain PQ.**
+3. Any active proof mode without >=128 conservative quantum bound? **No PQ-128 claim.**
+4. PoN quantum adversarial model absent? **No assertion of bounded quantum mining advantage.**
+5. Anti-rollback external trust not defined? **No durable PQ ownership guarantee.**
+6. No actual p99/DoS evidence? **No production-readiness assertion.**
